<title>PERU: Peru's Atacocha cut 1/3 of workforce-bolsa.</title>
<headline>Peru's Atacocha cut 1/3 of workforce-bolsa.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Minera Atacocha SA last month cut its workforce by almost a third in a voluntary redundancy program that costs $4 million, the Lima bolsa said on Friday.</p>
<p>The program reduced the polymetallic mining company's workforce by 201 employees. Atacocha, whose stock is currently leading the mining sector's record bull run on the bolsa, now employs 475 people, according to company officials.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
